        <h2>1) About Bridge</h2>
        <p>
          Bridge provides non-medical appointment execution support in Lincoln and Omaha, Nebraska. We help older adults with the logistics of medical visits, and keep their authorized family informed.
        </p>

        <h2>2) Services</h2>
        <p><strong>Primary service:</strong> Doctor / Hospital Appointment Support. Standard visit: $149, up to 2 hours, door to door. Extended or rural visit: $199. You pay Bridge directly; Bridge does not bill insurance or Medicare. First-visit guarantee: if your first visit doesn't go as promised, you don't pay.</p>
        <p>This service includes:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Pre-appointment confirmation</li>
          <li>Pickup at home</li>
          <li>Walk-in assistance</li>
          <li>Check-in support</li>
          <li>Waiting during the appointment</li>
          <li>Safe return home</li>
          <li>Text updates during the visit and a short written summary the same day (the Bridge Completion Report), sent to an authorized trusted contact</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3) Non-medical boundaries (Crucial)</h2>
        <p>Bridge and Bridge Captains <strong>do not</strong> provide the following:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>No medical advice</strong>, diagnosis, clinical interpretation, or treatment decisions.</li>
          <li>No medication administration, handling of prescriptions, or wound care.</li>
          <li>No physical lifting or transfer assistance (Bridge Captains may provide light stability support but cannot lift a person).</li>
          <li>No clinical advocacy or medical records management.</li>
          <li><strong>No emergency medical transport.</strong> In an emergency, call <strong>911</strong>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4) Bridge Completion Report</h2>
        <p>
          The Bridge Completion Report is a plain-language service update. It is <strong>not</strong> a medical record, diagnosis, clinical summary, or substitute for professional medical instructions. It is intended solely to verify that service steps (pickup, check-in, return) were completed.
        </p>

        <h2>5) Eligibility &amp; consent</h2>
        <p>
          By booking, you represent that you have authority to arrange the service. You confirm that the older adult being supported has consented to the service, and that you are authorized to share their information with Bridge. You also confirm that any trusted contact listed is authorized to receive the Completion Report.
        </p>

        <h2>6) Safety &amp; Captain discretion</h2>
        <p>
          Bridge Captains may stop or refuse service if conditions are unsafe or outside Bridge's non-medical scope. This includes requests for medical care, aggressive behavior, or environments that pose a risk to the Bridge Captain or the older adult. If an emergency occurs, the Bridge Captain will call 911.
        </p>

        <h2>7) Scheduling, timing, and wait</h2>
        <p>
          Appointment times can be unpredictable. The service includes waiting during the appointment unless the
          customer requests otherwise. Clinics can run late; your total duration may vary.
        </p>

        <h2>8) Payments, fees, and tips</h2>
        <p>
          Prices are shown at booking. Taxes may apply. Tips are optional unless required by law. Bridge
          facilitates payment and pays Bridge Captains.
        </p>

        <h2>9) Cancellations &amp; refunds</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cancel 24+ hours before</strong> scheduled pickup: full refund.</li>
          <li><strong>Cancel less than 24 hours</strong>: a cancellation fee may apply to compensate reserved Captain time.</li>
          <li><strong>No-show</strong> (Captain arrives and customer is unavailable): may be charged in full.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If Bridge cannot staff your appointment, you will not be charged (or you'll be refunded).
        </p>

        <h2>10) Customer responsibilities</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Provide an accurate pickup address, appointment location, and timing.</li>
          <li>Provide clear mobility and safety notes (e.g., walker use, stairs, pets).</li>
          <li>Ensure the older adult is ready for pickup at the scheduled time.</li>
          <li>Ensure the older adult brings ID, insurance cards, and any required appointment paperwork.</li>
          <li>Authorize Bridge to communicate with the designated trusted contact.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>11) Liability &amp; disclaimers</h2>
        <p>
          Bridge is not liable for clinical outcomes, missed diagnoses, provider decisions, or health
          complications. Transportation delays, clinic delays, weather, and third-party events can affect timing.
          To the extent permitted by law, Bridge disclaims all warranties and limits liability to the amount paid
          for the service in the prior 30 days.
        </p>

        <h2>12) Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Our Privacy Policy explains how we collect and use information. See <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>13) Changes to these Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms from time to time. The "Effective date" above reflects the latest version.
        </p>

        <h2>14) Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Call or text <a href="tel:+18159950115" data-track-loc="terms">815-995-0115</a>, or use our <a href="/book">request form</a>.
        </p>

